+- **Editorial headings and the wordmark treatment — UX candidate 14 October 2026:** Times New Roman where installed, then the already bundled Vietnamese Roboto, then serif fallback. The Windows audit found missing Vietnamese glyphs in Georgia and separated accents in headings. This candidate removes Georgia from the app token without downloading a font at runtime. On devices without Times New Roman, headings intentionally use Roboto until a licensed bundled serif is selected and verified. Keep regular weight, comfortable line height and unobstructed Vietnamese marks. This is a candidate change, not native-device acceptance or a change to exported logo artwork.
 - **Interface text:** Roboto on Android, native system sans on iOS, with a sans-serif fallback. Use 400–700 weights; reserve heavier weights for labels and active states.
 - **Number / practice timing:** interface sans by default; editorial serif can distinguish a single, prominent duration.
 - Do not set long copy in all caps. Eyebrow labels may use uppercase with generous tracking.
